{"t": 1794110901.6710472, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": ":rotating_light: Checkout paging (AG-7731, PaymentGatewayErrors)\n\nWhat's wrong: gateway 4xx rate ~38% since 07:41 UTC; charge calls are being rejected with 400 `invalid_amount`.\n\nRoot cause: the payment gateway switched to API 2026-11 (\"strict amounts\"), which requires `amount` as an integer in minor units (cents). Checkout was still sending a decimal euro amount (e.g. 12.34), so the gateway rejected it.\n\nFix: checkout/gateway.py now converts the EUR amount to integer cents before building the charge payload (12.34 EUR -> 1234). Verified locally; no behavior change for currency.\n\nStatus: fix committed to the working tree, not yet deployed. Next: roll out checkout, then confirm the gateway 4xx rate returns to baseline."}, "ok": true}
